      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE REHNQUIST: We'll hear argument now in No. 04-495, Reginald Wilkinson v. Charles E. Austin."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2004-04-495",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0e40339c5848c5031c20662a8432fe49d71fea699c9524c4fc3ef0dab00a7932",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0e40339c5848-0000-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: So there's -- there's no Eighth Amendment problem."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Deanne E. Maynard",
      "case_id": "2004-04-495",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0e40339c5848c5031c20662a8432fe49d71fea699c9524c4fc3ef0dab00a7932",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0e40339c5848-0001-0000",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "ORAL ARGUMENT OF DEANNE E. MAYNARD ON BEHALF OF THE UNITED STATES, AS AMICUS CURIAE, SUPPORTING THE PETITIONERS"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ohio",
      "case_id": "2004-04-495",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0e40339c5848c5031c20662a8432fe49d71fea699c9524c4fc3ef0dab00a7932",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0e40339c5848-0001-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The procedures that Ohio provides for placement into its supermax prison facility are more than ample to satisfy due process."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2004-04-495",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0e40339c5848c5031c20662a8432fe49d71fea699c9524c4fc3ef0dab00a7932",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0e40339c5848-0001-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: Why is it a predictive judgment that a person is a gang leader?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2004-04-495",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0e40339c5848c5031c20662a8432fe49d71fea699c9524c4fc3ef0dab00a7932",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0e40339c5848-0001-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KENNEDY: Well, those two, it seems to me, are all questions of -- of fact."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2004-04-495",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0e40339c5848c5031c20662a8432fe49d71fea699c9524c4fc3ef0dab00a7932",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0e40339c5848-0001-0004",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 26,
        "start": 26
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The injunction was entered by the Eastern District of Illinois and was affirmed by the Seventh Circuit in a case called Bono v. Saxby."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice O'Connor",
      "case_id": "2004-04-495",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "0e40339c5848c5031c20662a8432fe49d71fea699c9524c4fc3ef0dab00a7932",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0e40339c5848-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 37,
        "start": 37
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE O'CONNOR: Well, let -- you keep talking about what happened in the past, and I'm -- I find some difficulty with that because we're being asked to review a new policy. And I would like you to look at the new policy, show us where to find it in the record, and tell us specifically what's wrong with it."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Lobel",
      "case_id": "2004-04-495",
      "confidence": 0.93,
      "document_hash": "0e40339c5848c5031c20662a8432fe49d71fea699c9524c4fc3ef0dab00a7932",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0e40339c5848-0002-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Your Honor, it doesn't meet constitutional standards because it only says the chief has to make a final decision. The chief doesn't have to give any reasons for it, and I don't know of any case in this Court in predictive decisions, in punitive decisions where a -- a decision-maker can send somebody to solitary confinement long-term."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2004-04-495",
      "confidence": 0.94,
      "document_hash": "0e40339c5848c5031c20662a8432fe49d71fea699c9524c4fc3ef0dab00a7932",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0e40339c5848-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 39,
        "start": 39
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BREYER: So I think I've got your point. Tell me if I -- I mean, I've now looked at -- this is very confusing to me. I'm sure it's my fault. But I take it, if you look at page 22, that's the new policy."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Lobel",
      "case_id": "2004-04-495",
      "confidence": 0.92,
      "document_hash": "0e40339c5848c5031c20662a8432fe49d71fea699c9524c4fc3ef0dab00a7932",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0e40339c5848-0002-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 40,
        "start": 40
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Exactly. And that is why it's facially invalid."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2004-04-495",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "0e40339c5848c5031c20662a8432fe49d71fea699c9524c4fc3ef0dab00a7932",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0e40339c5848-0002-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 43,
        "start": 43
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KENNEDY: Could you comment on that?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Stevens",
      "case_id": "2004-04-495",
      "confidence": 0.91,
      "document_hash": "0e40339c5848c5031c20662a8432fe49d71fea699c9524c4fc3ef0dab00a7932",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0e40339c5848-0002-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 49,
        "start": 49
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE STEVENS: May I ask this question, Mr. Lobel? Putting aside for a second which policy we look at and so forth, were there findings that particular inmates were improperly sent to this facility?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2004-04-495",
      "confidence": 0.88,
      "document_hash": "0e40339c5848c5031c20662a8432fe49d71fea699c9524c4fc3ef0dab00a7932",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0e40339c5848-0002-0006",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 50,
        "start": 50
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the district court said you should give them new hearings following a procedure which would be sufficient to meet the constitutional Due Process Clause."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2004-04-495",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0e40339c5848c5031c20662a8432fe49d71fea699c9524c4fc3ef0dab00a7932",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0e40339c5848-0003-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 54,
        "start": 54
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: What does the new policy say about this?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Lobel",
      "case_id": "2004-04-495",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0e40339c5848c5031c20662a8432fe49d71fea699c9524c4fc3ef0dab00a7932",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0e40339c5848-0003-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 54,
        "start": 54
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "And what the district court ordered was draconian, that the classification chief, after he does this, without hearing from the inmate, without giving him reasons, has to write a final decision, which gives him some of the reasons that Mr. Roe is being kept there, and that they have to tell him, like they told the prisoners in -- in Greenholtz, what you have to do to get out."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2004-04-495",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0e40339c5848c5031c20662a8432fe49d71fea699c9524c4fc3ef0dab00a7932",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0e40339c5848-0003-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 55,
        "start": 55
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KENNEDY: Did they have reading materials?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "State officials",
      "case_id": "2004-04-495",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0e40339c5848c5031c20662a8432fe49d71fea699c9524c4fc3ef0dab00a7932",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0e40339c5848-0003-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 55,
        "start": 55
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The State officials testified that this was qualitatively different than any other prisoner, that the level of restriction, the no outdoor recreation for many years, that people have not been outside for years, the small cell with solid steel doors so that they could not hardly talk to anybody or see anybody, that these were conditions"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Lobel",
      "case_id": "2004-04-495",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0e40339c5848c5031c20662a8432fe49d71fea699c9524c4fc3ef0dab00a7932",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0e40339c5848-0003-0006",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 55,
        "start": 55
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. LOBEL: They had reading materials, yes, Your Honor, and they had televisions so they could watch their favorite programs."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioners",
      "case_id": "2004-04-495",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0e40339c5848c5031c20662a8432fe49d71fea699c9524c4fc3ef0dab00a7932",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0e40339c5848-0003-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 57,
        "start": 57
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "It has been pointed out that -- that inmates stay in the prison for many years, but in reality, over 600 inmates since the opening of -- of Ohio State penitentiary in 1998 -- over 600 inmates have gone into level 5 and over 550 inmates have left level 5. And so the classification process is an ongoing process."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2004-04-495",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0e40339c5848c5031c20662a8432fe49d71fea699c9524c4fc3ef0dab00a7932",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0e40339c5848-0003-0005",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 59,
        "start": 59
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the time of hearing, as incorporated in the notice to the inmate that a hearing will be held, and then an acknowledgement that there's -- only this evidence is the evidence that -- that is being relied upon really presents essentially a fact-finding hearing where the hearing process that is set forth in New Policy 111-07 is more than just fact-finding."
    }
  ],
  "schema_version": "1.0.0"
}
